From d4fc62428c4842817392d4bc7feb5d10c4c9a7aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/61] TSD / continuous FSD: also check the curves between
 sample points

Dominance was checked only at the merged sample points. That is exact
for discrete FSD (step functions) and SSD (LPM1 is piecewise linear),
but LPM2 is piecewise quadratic and the continuous FSD ratio
L1/(L1+U1) is linear-fractional between points, so the difference of
the two curves can peak strictly between knots. Both tests reported
false dominance, e.g. x = (-0.85,-1.52,0.68), y = (-0.21,-0.33,-1.67):
'X TSD Y' although LPM2_x - LPM2_y = +0.0389 at t = 0.16.

On each interval between knots the native pairwise test (used by the
.uni functions, the efficient set and SD.cluster) now also evaluates the
closed-form interior extremum: the vertex b/a of the quadratic when
a < 0 (TSD), and the stationary point of the difference of the two
linear-fractional ratios (continuous FSD). Candidates whose excess is at
rounding level (64 eps relative to the data scale) are ignored, so a
vertex that coincides with a knot does not reject a true dominance.
NNS.TSD and NNS.FSD(type = "continuous") take their verdict from the
same pairwise test in both directions (the grid curves are still used
for the plot).

Before -> after:
  8 TSD counterexamples (work/SDA/tsd_knots_counterex.json, exact
    interior excess 0.0013 .. 0.056): X TSD Y in 8 -> 0 (uni and NNS.TSD)
  continuous FSD x = (0.15,1.55,-0.86,-0.8,0.25,0.33),
    y = (-0.15,1.17,0.26,-0.04,-2.44,1.19): 'X FSD Y' -> 'NO FSD EXISTS'
  1500 random small normal pairs (seed 7): TSD positives 873 -> 873,
    continuous FSD positives 447 -> 446 (the one removed fails a dense
    grid check; none of the remaining positives does)
11-asset daily-return efficient sets (degrees 1-3, continuous) and the
0 / 15 / 15 FSD/SSD/TSD pair counts are unchanged.
